## IDs

| Id | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `P5-NNN` | Stable idea id in the P5 checklist (001–301) |
| `P3-NNN` | Stable idea id in the P3 checklist (001–238) |
| `PK-NNN` | Stable idea id in the Pokémon checklist (001–266) |
| `DB-NNN` | Stable idea id in the Dragon Ball checklist (001–244) |
| `IOS-NNN` | Stable idea id in the iOS & macOS checklist (001–258) |
| `AND-NNN` | Stable idea id in the Android checklist (001–417) |
| `SPX-NNN` | Registry `ref` in `entry.ts` / `index.ts` |

### Persona 5 refs

- Shipped P5 effects keep their **existing** refs (`P5-001`→`SPX-003`, `P5-002`→`SPX-012`, `P5-013`→`SPX-002`).
- Unbuilt P5 ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-015`…`SPX-312` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.

### Persona 3 refs

- Shipped P3 effects keep their **existing** refs (`P3-019` Blue Glass → `SPX-005`, `P3-037` Evoker Menu Snap → `SPX-006`).
- Unbuilt P3 ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-400`…`SPX-635` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.

### Pokémon refs

- Unbuilt PK ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-700`…`SPX-965` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.

### Dragon Ball refs

- Unbuilt DB ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-966`…`SPX-1209` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.

### iOS & macOS refs

- Unbuilt IOS ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-1300`…`SPX-1557` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.
- Legacy path [`docs/catalogue/ios_macos_effects_catalogue.md`](docs/catalogue/ios_macos_effects_catalogue.md) redirects to the canonical checklist.

### Android refs

- Unbuilt AND ideas are **pre-assigned** `SPX-1558`…`SPX-1974` — use that ref when implementing; do not invent a different number.
- Legacy path [`docs/catalogue/android_animation_effects_catalogue.md`](docs/catalogue/android_animation_effects_catalogue.md) redirects to the canonical checklist.

### Outside these catalogues

Non-catalogue specimens (other franchises / originals) take a free ref **not** reserved by an open `[ ]` P5, P3, PK, DB, IOS, or AND row — typically leftover `SPX-313`–`SPX-399`, `SPX-636`–`SPX-699`, `SPX-1210`–`SPX-1299`, or `SPX-1975+`.

## When a specimen ships

After a new specimen is registered with a real `ref` (same bar as `36_specimen-commits`):

1. Find its row in the matching checklist (`P5-NNN` / `P3-NNN` / `PK-NNN` / `DB-NNN` / `IOS-NNN` / `AND-NNN` / title / assigned `SPX-NNN`).
2. Flip **both** the master-list checkbox and the Core first-wave checkbox (if present) from `[ ]` to `[x]`.
3. Update the **Shipped** table and the **Progress** counts (`Done` / `Open` / `N / total`).
4. Remove a `· scaffold \`…\`` note once the specimen is fully registered.
5. Include the checklist edit in the specimen commit (or the same change set).

Do **not** mark `[x]` for scaffolds (`SPX-TODO`) or unregistered folders.

## Scope

Only applies to ideas listed in these six catalogue files. Other inspiration lineages do not use them.
